#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""freqs: one approve/reject sheet for the frequency catalog.

  freqs review          the sheet (~/Frequencies/catalog/review.csv), from the latest evidence
  freqs apply           your Approve/Reject marks applied to the catalog
  freqs config [--write]  what the radiod config would change; --write writes it
  freqs status          what's running, how much evidence there is, what's waiting

The evidence: activity's log (every transmission the receiver hears) and
tone-survey's results (the tone or digital mode of each), both running all
the time. review turns it into proposals, one a row:

  Change   a catalog channel heard with another tone, or digital
  Put on the air   a catalog channel not in the profile, heard as listed (confirmed)
  Remove   a catalog channel silent for days (not fire, EMS or other rare-use)
  Add      a downloaded listing (~/Frequencies/downloads) heard on the air, its
           tone or mode confirmed, at a frequency the catalog doesn't have yet;
           or (with activity -U) a busy frequency in no list, its tone or mode
           measured, under a placeholder name (Unknown 462.03125, Service Unknown)

Type Approve or Reject in the Decision column, save, close the sheet, and
run apply. Blank rows wait. A rejected proposal doesn't come back (unless
new evidence changes it). apply changes the catalog only: the radiod config
is rebuilt with config --write, when you choose, after seeing what changes.

Settings (all optional), in ~/Frequencies/freqs.conf:

  [freqs]
  catalog = ~/Frequencies/catalog
  downloads = ~/Frequencies/downloads
  sites = ~/Frequencies/downloads/sites   ; trunked systems' site lists: their channels aren't added
  activity = ~/activity.csv
  tones = ~/tone-survey.csv
  skip = GMRS|FRS          ; catalog channels never changed or removed (Service, Group or Name)
  profile = uhf            ; the catalog profile the radiod config is made from
  base = ~/Frequencies/uhf.d
  config = ~/Frequencies/uhf.d/50-conventional.conf
  names = ~/Frequencies/names/uhf-names.csv
"""
